{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "# Helper function: Reverses the first k elements of a list in-place.\ndef flip(lst: list, k: int) -> None:\n    left, right = 0, k - 1\n    while left < right:\n        lst[left], lst[right] = lst[right], lst[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n\n# Helper function: Finds the index of the maximum element in the first n elements.\ndef find_max_index(lst: list, n: int) -> int:\n    max_val = lst[0]\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if lst[i] > max_val:\n            max_val = lst[i]\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\n# Helper function: Validates if elements in the list are mutually comparable.\ndef validate_comparability(lst: list) -> None:\n    if len(lst) <= 1:\n        return\n    # Attempts to compare adjacent elements, raising TypeError if types are incompatible.\n    try:\n        for i in range(len(lst) - 1):\n            _ = lst[i] < lst[i+1]\n            _ = lst[i] == lst[i+1]\n    except (TypeError, AttributeError):\n        raise TypeError(\"Elements in the list are not mutually comparable.\")\n\ndef pancake_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list sorted in ascending (non-decreasing) order.\n    \"\"\"\n    work_list = list(input_list) # Create a shallow copy to avoid modifying the original list.\n\n    validate_comparability(work_list) # Validate element comparability before sorting.\n\n    n = len(work_list)\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in the current sublist (0 to current_size-1).\n        max_idx = find_max_index(work_list, current_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct position, perform flips.\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the front of the list.\n            flip(work_list, max_idx + 1)\n            # Move the maximum element from the front to its correct position.\n            flip(work_list, current_size)\n            \n    return work_list"}
